shape theory.physics.baryogenesis : theory.physics.neutrino, theory.physics.mirror {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Baryogenesis: Matter as a Gauge Choice (02d).
//
// The forcing chain:
//   1. Law of Persistence requires coherent projections to persist.
//   2. Without SU(2) unification, angular momentum cannot be
//      preserved -> structure cannot cohere.
//   3. Higgs (SU(2) unification) is REQUIRED, not optional.
//   4. Higgs defines forward chirality via 3-tick self-interference.
//   5. Law 2 forces balance -> mirror with opposite chirality.
//   6. Neutrinos carry the bias through forced chirality.
//   7. Weak interactions propagate it -> baryogenesis.
//
// Neutrinos are the ONLY particle with forced chirality. They
// traverse the SU(2)-complex through space. Right-handed neutrinos
// cannot exist in our projection (structurally impossible, not
// merely energetically unfavorable).
//
// The baryogenesis cascade:
//   1. Neutrinos ALWAYS left-handed in our universe.
//   2. Weak interactions involve neutrinos.
//   3. Particles interacting via weak force inherit left-handed bias.
//   4. This propagates through all weakly-interacting matter.
//   5. Baryons biased toward matter.
//   6. Matter had a statistical advantage. Matter won.
//
// The 10^-9 ratio measures how strongly weak interactions propagate
// the neutrino chirality bias. Two equivalent views:
//   Energy distribution: E_SU2 / E_total ~ 10^-9
//   Neutrino cascade: ~10^-9 coupling efficiency
//
// "Left" is just a name. The mirror universe has the same physics,
// same chemistry, same observers. They call their stuff "matter."
// Matter-antimatter distinction is a gauge choice frozen by the Higgs.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.neutrino (forced chirality),
//               theory.physics.mirror (forced mirror structure)
  """
}
